- op: discuss  # 7abb
  at: '2026-04-28T05:51:46Z'  # 7abb
  by: agent  # 7abb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7abb
  clock: 5  # 7abb
  nonce: 7abb  # 7abb
  message: "Merged in PR #157 (commit 57954fae5). Implementation:\n\n1. Added `compute_dampened_centrality(symbols, edges, *, ...)` in ranking.py — single source of truth for the canonical 8-stage stack.\n2. Added internal `_apply_canonical_dampeners` so rank_symbols can keep raw_centrality separate while still sharing the dampener logic.\n3. Refactored 3 full-stack call sites: sketch._format_symbols (passes `exclude_dampeners=(\"file_kind\",)`), compact.select_by_coverage, compact.select_by_connectivity (centrality-is-None branch).\n4. Refactored format_tiered_behavior_map's victim-removal step using a new `_VICTIM_REMOVAL_EXCLUDE_DAMPENERS` constant — this makes \"tier-only victim ordering\" explicit instead of a silent omission.\n5. Left select_by_tokens (compact.py:1134) untouched: it intentionally uses untuned compute_centrality for coverage normalization, not selection ranking.\n\nNo behavior change — all 4,293 tests pass at 100% coverage. Net diff: +278/-134 lines (refactor extracts shared logic and removes duplication).\n\nTests added in test_ranking.py::TestComputeDampenedCentrality cover: empty input, full-stack identity vs inline replication, first_party_priority skip-tier semantics, exclude_dampeners opt-out (file-kind), and default-vs-explicit-tuned-params equivalence."  # 7abb
